msgid "Adding new events"
msgstr ""

msgid "This section is for extension authors who want to add new JFR events."
msgstr ""

msgid "Depending on the API module"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus JFR extension separates the public API from the runtime "
"implementation.\n"
"As a result, other extensions can implement JFR-based instrumentation by "
"depending only on the JFR API module, without adding a dependency on the "
"Quarkus JFR extension implementation itself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At deployment time, an extension can detect whether the application has "
"enabled the Quarkus JFR extension by using Quarkus capabilities:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This pattern allows your extension to:\n"
"* compile against stable API types only, and\n"
"* activate JFR instrumentation only when the Quarkus JFR extension is "
"present in the application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Associating events by request"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that new events be associated with existing events.\n"
"Associations are useful when looking at the details of a process that is "
"taking a long time.\n"
"For example, a general REST application retrieves the data needed for "
"processing from a datastore.\n"
"If REST events are not associated with datastore events, it is impossible to "
"know which datastore events were processed in each REST request.\n"
"When the two events are associated, we know immediately which datastore "
"event was processed in each REST request."
msgstr ""

msgid "Datastore events are not implemented yet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus JFR extension provides a Request ID for event association.\n"
"See <<identifying-requests>> for more information on Request IDs."
msgstr ""

msgid "In code, you typically need the following two steps."
msgstr ""

msgid "1) Add trace/span identifiers to your event"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implement `traceId` and `spanId` on the new event as follows.\n"
"The `@TraceIdRelational` and `@SpanIdRelational` annotations mark these "
"fields as relational identifiers used for association."
msgstr ""

msgid "2) Populate the identifiers from the IdProducer"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Obtain the values to store in the event from an `IdProducer` and set them "
"just before committing the event."
msgstr ""

